    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the \"create meaning\" thing in theory but it feels like a lot of extra work just to delay the inevitable. if we're talking strictly logically, though, if the outcome is always zero, why is the \"effort\" of living a requirement? it seems more efficient to just reach the zero state now. it's a perfectly logical equilibrium, isn't it?",
